 "text": "In 1960, an FDA reviewer refused a pill sold in dozens of countries. It was thaladomide. Why did she say no? Frances Kelsey found its safety evidence too thin. The company kept pressing. She kept asking for reliable evidence. Then researchers linked it to severe birth defects. It was never marketed in the U .S. Lesson popularity isn't proof of safety. Ask what the evidence shows. Download RM to support livelihood tools."
